}","title":"Kotlin/Wasm JavaScript interoperability","source":"https://kotlinlang.org/docs/wasm-js-interop.html","sections":["Interoperability with JavaScript > Use JavaScript code in Kotlin > JavaScript modules"],"line_start":180,"line_end":206,"score":0.6052181720733643,"release_version":null,"availability":"unknown"},{"anchor":"js-interop.md","start":0,"end":564,"split_code":false,"platforms":["js"],"id":"c2","document_id":"js-interop","strategy":"semantic","text":"Use JavaScript code from Kotlin

Kotlin was first designed for easy interoperation with the Java platform: it sees Java classes as Kotlin classes, and Java sees Kotlin classes as Java classes.

However, JavaScript is a dynamically typed language, which means it does not check types at compile time. You can freely talk to JavaScript from Kotlin via dynamic types. If you want to use the full power of the Kotlin type system, you can create external declarations for JavaScript libraries which will be understood by the Kotlin compiler and the surrounding tooling.","title":"Use JavaScript code from Kotlin","source":"https://kotlinlang.org/docs/js-interop.html","sections":["Use JavaScript code from Kotlin"],"line_start":1,"line_end":5,"score":0.5972615480422974,"release_version":null,"availability":"unknown"}]}

